# The vendored SO-101 model is FINGERPRINTED, so its bytes must not depend on the platform.
#
# tests/test_arm_config.py::test_vendored_model_fingerprint pins the sha256 of scene.xml and
# so101_new_calib.xml, because a silent asset swap changes the physics under every torque and
# limit assertion in the suite. Without an attribute here, git applied its default eol handling
# to those two files: measured, the working copy was 23 and 165 bytes LARGER than the stored
# blob on Windows, purely from CRLF. The pin was therefore computed on one platform and could
# never match a checkout on another -- CI failed on exactly this, and the failure was real: a
# fingerprint that changes with the checkout is not a fingerprint.
#
# `-text` means "store and check out these bytes verbatim, on every platform".
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/so101/*.xml -text
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/so101/SO-ARM100-LICENSE -text

# The meshes were ALREADY safe -- git auto-detected them as binary and left them byte-identical
# (blob size == working size, verified per file). This makes that a guarantee rather than a
# lucky detection: an STL is a header plus packed floats, and 0d 0a occurs in that data by
# coincidence, so anything that "helpfully" translated it would corrupt geometry silently.
*.stl binary

# The perception packs vendored for CI are zip containers; never translate them.
*.npz binary
native/sndl-core/tests/fixtures_rng.json -text

# The safety envelope's five files are HASHED by gates/envelope_hash_gate.py from their working bytes, so their bytes must
# not depend on the platform either (policy audit pa-p5env-1: the baseline held 3 CRLF-checkout and 2 LF-blob hashes, so
# the gate was red on any fresh checkout). eol=lf makes every checkout hold the stored LF blob; the baseline holds the LF
# blob hashes. Owner, verbatim, in chat 2026-10-24: "Yes, approve the envelope-hash line-ending fix".
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/reflex.py text eol=lf
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/serial_arm.py text eol=lf
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/so101_arm.py text eol=lf
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/arm_config.py text eol=lf
src/snn_data_lake/brainstem/interpreter.py text eol=lf
